Details:
Endpoint: GET `/wp-json/tutor/v1/students/{id}/courses`

If anyone tries to request this endpoint with the student id who is not enrolled in any course yet.  Then it return's an error message.
```{
"code":"tutor_read_student",
"message":"Courses retrieved failed",
"data":{
"status":500,
"details":"count(): Argument #1 ($value) must be of type Countable|array, false given"
}
} ```
Instead this should be return a meaning full message like: *This student is not enrolled in any course yet.*

2FA login OTP email template does not process the {site_url} place holder please load it correctly.

This should be image permalink but it does not resolve from the function thus the placeholder loading in plain text format.

Reference File: `wp-content/plugins/tutor-pro/addons/auth/templates/email/login-otp.php`
Function call from: `wp-content/plugins/tutor-pro/addons/auth/classes/Utils.php` 

```public static function sent_login_otp($email, $otp)
    {
        $email_tpl = tutor_auth()->templates . 'email/login-otp.php';
        // translators: %s is the site name.
        $subject = sprintf(__('%s - Login OTP', 'tutor-pro'), get_bloginfo('name'));
        $site_url   = get_bloginfo('url');

        $data = array(
            '{login_otp}'            => $otp,
            '{testing_email_notice}' => '',
            '{footer_text}'          => tutor_pro_email_global_footer(),
            '{additional_footer}'    => __('This is an automatically generated email. Please do not reply to this email.', 'tutor-pro'),
        );

        $message = Mailer::prepare_template($email_tpl, $data);
        return Mailer::send_mail($email, $subject, $message);
    } ```
